homelab-cli (0.2.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add a `--config DIR` global flag (also $HOMELAB_CLI_CONFIG_DIR) to
    override the default ~/.config/homelab-cli/ session/config directory
    -- needed for service accounts (homelab-backup-client/-server) so
    their sessions never collide with a human's.
  * `login` supports non-interactive use via --password, --password-stdin,
    or --password-env VAR (requires --email alongside any of them --
    otherwise falls back to the existing interactive prompts).
  * New `backup` command group: enroll, list-pending-enrollments,
    ack-enrollment, revoke-host, report-run, report-check, list-hosts,
    list-repos, host-runs, server-info, set-server-info -- the control-
    plane surface for homelab-backup-client/-server's redesigned
    enrollment/bookkeeping flow.
  * New `admin create-user` (idempotent account creation, prints a
    server-generated password once) and `admin list-users` (every
    account's roles + active flag).
  * Tab completion is now generated from this script's own argparse tree
    via argcomplete instead of a hand-maintained bash file (which had
    already drifted out of sync more than once) -- also picks up
    flag-prefix and choices= completion for free. New Depends:
    python3-argcomplete, bash-completion.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sat, 29 Aug 2026 14:59:25 -0500

homelab-cli (0.2.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix bash completion: --attach-file, --attach-drive, --cc, --bcc,
    --html, and --in-reply-to were missing from the value-flags list, so
    tab-completing a value after --attach-file produced nothing instead
    of local filenames. --attach-file now completes local paths (like
    --output); --attach-drive correctly offers no completions, since it
    takes a remote numeric Drive file id.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sat, 22 Aug 2026 12:36:17 -0500

homelab-cli (0.2.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add `mail send`, `mail draft`, and `mail allowed-from` commands.
    `send`/`draft` support --to/--cc/--bcc (repeatable), --body/--html,
    --attach-file (repeatable local upload), --attach-drive (repeatable,
    numeric Drive file id, no re-upload; a directory id is rejected as
    not-yet-implemented), and --in-reply-to FOLDER:UID for reply
    threading.
  * Add `drive list-files` as a plain alias for `drive file-info` (same
    handler, same args) for discoverability.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sat, 22 Aug 2026 12:13:42 -0500

homelab-cli (0.2.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add `mail search`, `mail flags`, `mail move`, `mail trash`, `mail
    purge`, and `mail folder-create`/`folder-rename`/`folder-delete`
    commands, wrapping the new mutating mail endpoints. `trash` moves a
    message to the account's Trash (recoverable); `purge` permanently
    deletes a message but only works on one already in Trash and has no
    --folder option, since it can never target a live mailbox.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sat, 22 Aug 2026 09:00:00 -0500

homelab-cli (0.2.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add `mail folders`, `mail messages`, `mail message`, and `mail part`
    commands, wrapping the new GET /api/v1/mail/{folders,messages,
    messages/:uid,messages/:uid/part} endpoints. A message's content is
    exposed as a flat list of MIME parts (no single "body" field) --
    `mail part` fetches any specific part's content by number, text or
    binary alike. Updated homelab-cli-mail(8).

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Fri, 21 Aug 2026 19:15:00 -0500

